---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SafetyNotice from '../components/SafetyNotice.astro';
import { pageTitle, breadcrumbJsonLd } from '../lib/seo';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={pageTitle('Safety')}
  description="Practical safety rules for using community directory listings."
  canonicalPath="/safety/"
  jsonLd={breadcrumbJsonLd([{ name: 'Safety', path: '/safety/' }])}
>
  <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-900 sm:text-3xl">Safety</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-stone-600">A short, practical guide to staying safe when exploring community listings.</p>

    <SafetyNotice class="mt-6" />

    <div class="prose-static mt-8">
      <h2>The basics</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Directory listings are external.</strong> Every listing points to
          a community hosted by someone else. Inclusion is not an endorsement.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Evaluate before you join.</strong> Look at the community's pinned
          messages, admin behavior and public history before sharing anything.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Never share passwords, recovery phrases or private keys</strong> —
          in any group, for any reason, regardless of who asks.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Be skeptical of guaranteed profits.</strong> “100% win rate”,
          “risk-free returns”, “double your money” — these are not real. Treat them
          as red flags, not opportunities.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Verify administrators independently.</strong> Anyone can copy a
          username or avatar. Confirm identities through the platform's official
          channels before trusting instructions.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Don't send money based on a listing.</strong> If a community asks
          for payment to join or “unlock” access, treat that with extreme caution.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Financial communities</h2>
      <p>
        Communities that discuss crypto, forex, stocks or earning money vary wildly
        in quality and intent. Our listings distinguish education, discussion, news
        and signals — but even an “education” label is not a guarantee. Verify any
        claim independently, and never trade with money you cannot afford to lose.
      </p>

      <h2>What we check — and what we don't</h2>
      <p>
        We check whether invite links appear to work, and we record honest
        verification states (<a href="/how-we-verify/">see How We Verify</a>).
        We do <strong>not</strong> audit community content, members, admins or
        financial claims. A checked link is a working link — nothing more.
      </p>

      <h2>Report problems</h2>
      <p>
        See a dead invite, scam behavior, or misleading information? Use the{' '}
        <a href="/report/">report form</a> — every report is reviewed by a human.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
